# Changes

## 0.2.1 - 2026-09-03

* Treats the loaded profile/`ASGS_CONFIG` as the durable monitored identity and
  the `asgs_main.sh` PID as transient runtime state.
* Matches the real `asgs_main.sh -c <canonical ASGS_CONFIG>` argv structure
  instead of basename/substring config matches.
* Revalidates `/proc` candidates and debounces transient Bash fork/subshell
  duplicates before declaring multiple ASGS processes.
* Removes surviving descendant candidates when another matching candidate is
  their ancestor.
* Allows the monitor to start/remain alive while ASGS is absent and
  automatically reacquires a new PID after restart under the same profile.
* Exports process lifecycle state through `ASGS_MON_PROCESS_*`, includes it in
  status/adapter JSON, and clears stale `ASGS_PID` values while waiting.
* `000-asgs_main-pid-check` now reports waiting/ambiguity/restart lifecycle
  state supplied by the supervisor; restart recovery is an immediate NOTICE.
* Added process discovery/debounce and restart/reacquisition regression tests.

## 0.2.0 - 2026-09-01

* Hardened process detection around the loaded `ASGS_CONFIG`; ambiguous matches
  now require `--pid` instead of selecting the lowest PID.
* Added one-monitor-per-profile locking.
* Replaced shell-string check execution and sendmail invocation with list-form
  process execution.
* Enforced per-check timeouts and normalized bad/empty check results to UNKNOWN.
* Changed notification throttling to transition/escalation/hush semantics so
  persistent CRITICAL conditions do not email every monitor pass.
* Refreshes ASGS state each pass and exports normalized `ASGS_MON_*` context.
* Retained the legacy eight positional plugin arguments.
* Added `--once`, `--check`, `--list`, `--enable`, `--disable`, `--validate`,
  and `--status`.
* Running monitors now rescan `active/` each pass, so check enable/disable
  changes take effect without restart.
* Expanded the Bash helper into a robust check API with safe color setup,
  alert helpers, requirements, scheduling, file-age helpers, and compatibility
  accessors.
* Removed state-file `source`/evaluation from Bash helpers/checks.
* Fixed known check issues: JSON warnings on STDOUT, queue state output,
  STATEFILE error status, RUNDIR unit reporting, failed-dir diagnostics,
  SYSLOG rotation/truncation, quoting/word splitting, and TTY handling.
* Added atomic heartbeat/status JSON for external supervision and
  `asgs-mon --status`.
* Added a disabled-by-default adapter seam and JSONL example for future central
  dashboard integration.
* Added check templates, tests, CI, and an optional ASGS `fetch` integration
  patch.
* Uses `Util::H2O::More` conservatively for options/config/runtime objects and
  `Dispatch::Fu` for top-level command dispatch.
